+# Test fixtures — provenance
+
+Pinned vendor bytes for suites that must not *synthesise* the shape they then parse.
+Each file records where it came from, and which of its claims are **OBSERVED** (copied
+out of a real record) versus **DERIVED** (constructed from the shipped binary's own
+mapping). A fixture nobody can trace is a fixture nobody can trust.
+
+Consumer: `template/tests/test_terminal_error_classification.py` (issue #506). Every
+criterion there is also covered by a case that builds its events **inline**, so the suite
+still asserts the rule when these files are absent — a fixture-replaying case skips
+itself rather than erroring.
+
+## `claude_api_error_death.transcript.jsonl` — OBSERVED, verbatim
+
+One line, copied byte-for-byte out of the Claude Code session transcript of the
+**issue #506 incident**: the escalated builder of `getwyrd/wyrd-pdca`
+`results/issue_717/` ran ~18 minutes, the API connection dropped mid-response, and the
+CLI exited 1. Source file:
+
+    ~/.claude/projects/-home-eddie-wyrd-wyrd-pdca/31fa2f21-4d73-4810-9c23-ba33bd860167.jsonl
+
+line 345 — the session's last event (line 346 is the CLI's own `last-prompt` bookkeeping
+record, not a stream event), written by claude-code **2.1.228**, `"entrypoint":
+"sdk-cli"` (i.e. the headless `claude -p` the Do leaf spawns). Re-verified against the
+file on 2026-08-16.
+
+What matters in it, and why the classifier reads *these* and not the prose:
+
+* `"type": "assistant"` — so `progress._is_session_event` counts it as **substantive
+  work**. That is precisely why "did it produce anything?" misclassified this death;
+* `"isApiErrorMessage": true` — the CLI **marks** the message it synthesises for an API
+  failure. A leaf that merely *writes about* an API error never carries this flag, so the
+  mark, not the wording, is the discriminator;
+* `"error": "server_error"` — the CLI's own error *kind*, and the transient half of
+  `progress._CLAUDE_TRANSIENT_ERROR_KINDS`;
+* `"model": "<synthetic>"` — the message was manufactured locally, not returned by a model;
+* the single text block, `API Error: Connection lost mid-response. The response above may
+  be incomplete.` — the diagnostic that existed **only** here, and never in the bundle,
+  before #506.
+
+## `claude_api_error_permanent.transcript.jsonl` — OBSERVED, verbatim
+
+The counter-example, from a second real session (`~/.claude/projects/`
+`-home-eddie-pdca-pdca-pdca/152ac920-829e-452d-8dca-a87c28819d7e.jsonl` line 7,
+claude-code **2.1.222**, `entrypoint: sdk-cli`): a marked API-error message the vendor
+classified **permanent** — `"error": "model_not_found"`, `"apiErrorStatus": 404`. It is
+retained like any other marked report and must **not** be retried. It also shows that the
+persisted record carries `apiErrorStatus` even though the stream's `assistant` emitter
+does not forward it (below).
+
+## `*.stream.jsonl` — DERIVED (labelled, not observed)
+
+The same records as the CLI's `--output-format stream-json` writer emits them on
+**stdout** — the bytes `progress.run_with_heartbeat` actually parses. They are *derived*,
+not captured: inducing a real mid-response connection loss (or a 404 model) on demand is
+not something a test can do, so each is generated from the transcript record above by the
+CLI's own transcript → stream mapping for an `assistant` event, read out of the shipped
+binary (claude-code **2.1.233**, `~/.local/share/claude/versions/2.1.233`):
+
+```js
+case "assistant": { … return [{ type: "assistant", message: n, session_id: qt(),
+  parent_tool_use_id: null, uuid: r.uuid, timestamp: r.timestamp, error: r.error,
+  ...(r.requestId !== undefined && { request_id: r.requestId }),
+  ...(r.isAbortedMidStream && { aborted: true }),
+  ...(r.isApiErrorMessage === true && { is_api_error_message: true }), … }] }
+```
+
+Note the **key rename**: the persisted transcript spells the flag `isApiErrorMessage`,
+the stream spells it `is_api_error_message`. `progress._terminal_error` accepts both
+spellings for exactly this reason: keying on one of them would leave the incident unfixed
+with the suite green. Note too what the emitter above does **not** write: the SDK schema
+declares `api_error_status` ("HTTP status code of the API error") and `api_error` as
+optional siblings of the flag, but 2.1.233 attaches neither to an `assistant` event — so a
+rule reading them there is a branch that looks like coverage and is not. The status reaches
+the stream on the `result` wrap-up instead (below).
+
+Regenerate after re-pinning a transcript line:
+
+```python
+rec = json.loads(Path("<name>.transcript.jsonl").read_text())
+stream = {"type": "assistant", "message": rec["message"], "session_id": rec["sessionId"],
+          "parent_tool_use_id": None, "uuid": rec["uuid"], "timestamp": rec["timestamp"],
+          "error": rec["error"]}
+if rec.get("requestId") is not None:
+    stream["request_id"] = rec["requestId"]
+if rec.get("isApiErrorMessage") is True:
+    stream["is_api_error_message"] = True
+```
+
+## What the classifier keys on, READ FROM THE BINARY (2.1.233), not fixture bytes
+
+No transcript records a `result` event (it goes to stdout only), and no transcript here
+records a subagent's stream framing, so those shapes are quoted from the engine that emits
+them — checkable rather than asserted:
+
+```js
+// the session wrap-up
+_t = jt===null && Xr===void 0 && Ue                        // turns exhausted
+   ? ite({common:{is_error:!0}, variant:{subtype:"error_max_turns",
+        errors:[`Reached maximum number of turns (${Ue.maxTurns})`]}})
+   : Jr!==null                     // Jr = [thrown error] | ["[ede_diagnostic] turn
+   ? ite({common:{is_error:!0},    //       aborted (<reason>) stop_reason=<x>"]
+        variant:{subtype:"error_during_execution", errors:Jr}})
+   : ite({common:{is_error:Ze},    // Ze = isApiErrorMessage, gt = apiErrorStatus ?? null
+        variant:{subtype:"success", api_error_status:gt, result:Ze?Dt:qe}});
+```
+
+So `is_error` on a **`success`** result is the CLI saying "this session ended on my own
+API-error message", and that variant alone carries `api_error_status`; the `error_*`
+variants carry a free `errors: string[]` instead and name no cause, which is why the
+wrap-up never overwrites the report before it (`progress._note_terminal`).
+
+```js
+// a SUBAGENT's messages, emitted through the agent_progress branch
+case "progress": if (e.data.type === "agent_progress" || e.data.type === "skill_progress") {
+  … yield {type:"assistant", message: a, parent_tool_use_id: e.parentToolUseID,
+    session_id: qt(), uuid: i.uuid, timestamp: i.timestamp, error: i.error,
+    ...(i.requestId !== undefined && {request_id: i.requestId}),
+    ...(n !== undefined && {subagent_type: n}), ...(o !== undefined && {task_description: o}),
+    ...(i.isApiErrorMessage === true && {is_api_error_message: true}), … } }
+```
+
+versus the main loop's own emitters, which hard-code `parent_tool_use_id: null`. Note the
+last spread: **the mark is forwarded for a subagent too**, so `is_api_error_message` alone
+does not say whose death it was — `parent_tool_use_id` does. That one field carries both
+halves of the scope rule in `progress.py`: only the MAIN session carrying on clears a
+terminal report (`_is_main_session_work`, so one trailing subagent line cannot erase the
+account of the death), and only the MAIN session's own report may classify
+(`_terminal_error`, so a trailing subagent report cannot overwrite it and relabel a
+permanent cause transient).
+
+That asymmetry is the vendor's, not ours: 2.1.233 **recovers** from a subagent's API-error
+termination itself rather than ending the session —
+
+```js
+class dvi extends kt { errorKind; constructor(e,t){
+  super(`Agent terminated early due to an API error: ${e}`, …); this.name =
+  "AgentApiErrorTerminationError" } }
+bJv = new Set(["rate_limit","overloaded","server_error"]);
+function vJv(e,t){ if(!(e instanceof dvi)) return null;
+  if(!e.errorKind || !bJv.has(e.errorKind)) return null;
+  let r = t.filter((n)=> n.type!=="assistant" || !n.isApiErrorMessage);
+  if(L4r(r)===void 0) return null;
+  return {history:r, cutoffNote: `${…}` + "Everything below is PARTIAL output recovered "
+    + "from the agent before it was cut off. The agent did NOT finish its task …"} }
+```
+
+— i.e. a Task that hit a 529 hands the main loop partial output and the session carries on.
+So "a subagent reported an API error" is evidence to keep, never the leaf's verdict; a
+subagent report is retained with the `[sub-agent report, not the leaf's own death]` prefix
+and is never transient (`progress._SUBAGENT_REPORT`).
+
+**No subagent record is pinned here, deliberately.** Every `isApiErrorMessage` record in
+the transcripts available on this machine is a main-session one (`isSidechain: false`) —
+the two pinned above — so a "subagent api-error" fixture would be a shape *we* invented
+wearing a fixture's authority. The subagent framing is therefore DERIVED only, from the
+emitter quoted above, and the suite builds those events **inline** where it needs them
+(`test_terminal_error_classification.subagent_report`).
+
+Two more constants are read from the same binary:
+
+* the vendor's own transient test — `isTransient: t.apiErrorIsTransient === !0 ||
+  t.error === "overloaded" || t.error === "server_error"` — and, for a subagent's
+  API-error termination, `new Set(["rate_limit","overloaded","server_error"])`. Together
+  they are `progress._CLAUDE_TRANSIENT_ERROR_KINDS`. `apiErrorIsTransient` itself is
+  **not** forwarded to the stream by any emitter above, which is why the kinds carry it;
+* the full kind enum — `["authentication_failed","oauth_org_not_allowed","billing_error",
+  "rate_limit","overloaded","invalid_request","model_not_found","server_error","unknown",
+  "max_output_tokens"]` — whose non-transient, non-`unknown` members are
+  `progress._CLAUDE_PERMANENT_ERROR_KINDS`. Only `unknown` reaches the category regex:
+  the mapper's last resort is `Yd({content: "API Error: " + e.message, error: "unknown"})`,
+  taken when a plain `Error`'s cause code is in neither of its connection-code sets
+  (`["ECONNREFUSED","ConnectionRefused","ENOTFOUND","ENETUNREACH","ENETDOWN",
+  "EHOSTUNREACH","EHOSTDOWN","EAI_AGAIN","FailedToOpenSocket","ERR_PROXY_TUNNEL"]` and
+  `["ECONNRESET","EPIPE","ConnectionClosed","ETIMEDOUT","ECONNABORTED","ERR_SOCKET_CLOSED",
+  "StreamSuspended"]`) — neither holds any `UND_ERR_*`, so a fetch aborted mid-body
+  arrives as `API Error: terminated` with no kind at all.
